## 5. Generated outputs and third-party rights

Flashcards and other outputs independently generated by using the Software do **not** automatically become owned by the Licensor or subject to the repository's content license solely because the Software was used. However, commercial use of the Software to produce those outputs still requires advance written authorization under Section 3.

A later change of purpose alone does not retroactively turn a genuinely permitted noncommercial use into a violation. This License does not impose a separate restriction on later commercial distribution of independently generated outputs that contain no protected repository material. However, further use of the Software to edit, expand, regenerate, or batch-produce outputs for a commercial purpose requires advance authorization. An asserted personal purpose does not exempt generation that was objectively intended for a commercial business or distribution from the outset. Outputs incorporating protected repository material remain subject to that material's applicable license.

This License does not grant rights in third-party textbooks, vocabulary lists, trademarks, images, model-generated content, or other external materials. Their separate terms and applicable laws remain in effect.

## 6. Commercial licensing

For commercial authorization, open an issue at https://github.com/chaogevision/words-flashcard/issues/new and describe the organization, intended use, distribution channel, expected scale, and contact method. An inquiry or an unanswered request does not itself grant permission. Only express written authorization from the rights holder grants additional rights. That authorization should identify the authorized legal person or entity, permitted uses, duration, organizational or seat scope, output distribution rights, and any sublicensing rights; no such rights should be inferred from an inquiry or silence.

